    description: "WHAT FAILS. The full-suite cron's `self-claims-gate` step (pipeline 4141, dev cc4ab781, 2026-10-02) reports SELF-CLAIM DRIFT on all 18 self-claims: verdict confirmed_with_caveats -> inconclusive, caveat opaque_boundary dropped. Every claim's details name the blocker: \"it makes calls into 1 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify (rich.text.Text), which is what withholds the qualified verdict the launches alone would have earned.\"\n\nCAUSE, bisected locally (verify-claims --json --minimal, each arm cold on its own XDG_CACHE_HOME, compared with that arm's snapshot by scripts/check-self-claims-drift):\n    a92e231a93 (parent of WI-sugom)  OK, 18 claims unchanged\n    f592cb04dc (WI-sugom, 09-28)     18 claims drifted (36 changed lines)\n    8cfcab7b07 (pre-run0930), 31a63b2b65, e3a3c7a809, c8754df23d: all drifted identically\nWI-sugom made a from-imported owner resolve to its module, so tracker/tui.py's `from rich.text import Text as RichText` types RichText.from_markup(...) (5 sites) and Text.from_markup(...).plain as calls into the CLASS rich.text.Text. docs/io-primitives-overlays/hypergumbo-self.yaml declares the module rich.text only; completeness matching is exact; `qualifying_only = not unknown`, so one unclassified class withholds every qualified verdict. The analyzer change is correct (ADR-0059: a call on the type itself); the overlay is what lagged.\n\nThis is the FOURTH instance of the WI-jabus shape (uvicorn, then the WI-jabus class-qualified receivers, now this). Not a run0930 regression.\n\nFIX: add `rich.text.Text` (completeness: complete, with the reason) to the self overlay. No snapshot or SECURITY.md change: the verdicts return to what both already say.\n\nNOT ADDRESSED HERE (the family): any receiver-typing gain can turn a class slot under a declared module into an unknown module and withhold all 18 claims. The gate is cron-only by design (woodpecker.yml ~324-358), so detection is up to ~12 h after merge, and this one sat red for ~4 days (09-28 -> 10-02) without anyone reading `ci-debug cron-status`."  # 314d
